---
title: "Phase 4: Data Preparation and Metadata Creation"
---
flowchart TD
    sub["Data Publication Workflow | Data preparation and metadata creation can run in parallel with each other"]:::subtitle
    r10["<b>R10 (Horizontal Requirement — all phases):</b> Track provenance of all AI agent actions on data and metadata. Record all actions so they can be verified, validated and audited."]:::horizontal
    sub ~~~ r10 ~~~ phase4

    phase4["PHASE 4: DATA PREPARATION AND METADATA CREATION"]:::phase
    clean["Clean, organise and version files"]:::step
    convert["Convert to open or non-proprietary formats (OPTIONAL)<br><br><b>Guidance note:</b> The agent could recommend formats and tools but does not perform conversion for large collections or complex pipelines. The researcher carries out conversion outside the agent where needed.<br><br><b>R3:</b> Suggest appropriate vocabularies, ontologies and open data formats"]:::step
    dict{"Was a data dictionary and README file created pre-collection?"}:::decision
    update["Review and update data dictionary and README file for data publication"]:::step
    create["Create data dictionary and README file<br><br><b>R5:</b> Draft data documentation including READMEs and data dictionaries at publication"]:::step
    standard["Identify metadata standard (usually dictated by repository) e.g. Dublin Core, DataCite"]:::step
    vocab["Finalise controlled vocabularies and ontologies"]:::step
    complete["Complete metadata fields in repository deposit form<br><br><b>R6:</b> Enable interoperable metadata across institutions and Data Director instances<br><br><b>R2:</b> Generate FAIR-aligned and discipline-appropriate metadata using controlled vocabularies, ontologies and community standards including CARE principles"]:::step
    next["→ Continues to Phase 5: Deposit and Submit (see next page)"]:::link

    phase4 --> clean --> convert --> dict
    dict -- YES --> update
    dict -- NO --> create
    update --> standard
    create --> standard
    standard --> vocab --> complete --> next

